<title>ISRAEL: Israel's April foreign currency reserves a record.</title>
<headline>Israel's April foreign currency reserves a record.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves at the end of April rose to a record $16.011 billion, the Bank of Israel said on Thursday.</p>
<p>		 (in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>		 April 1997	March 1997     April 1996</p>
<p>Reserves     16.011	    15.336	   9.451</p>
<p>The central bank attributed the increase to activities of the non-financial private sector and to foreign currency loans the private sector took at Israeli banks.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
